1
00:00:00,167 --> 00:00:03,337
(Past Sheldon:)No. But your ability to
perceive their existence is conditional...

2
00:00:06,757 --> 00:00:09,757
(Past Leonard:)-There's three?
-Each more daunting than the last.

3
00:00:11,345 --> 00:00:13,685
(Past Sheldon:)-Have a seat.
-Okay.

4
00:00:14,348 --> 00:00:16,688
No, that's where I sit.

5
00:00:20,646 --> 00:00:21,856
(Past Leonard:)What's the difference?

6
00:00:22,022 --> 00:00:24,192
(Past Sheldon:)This seat is ideally located...

7
00:00:24,358 --> 00:00:28,108
(Past Sheldon:)...in relation to the heat source in the
winter and a cross breeze in the summer.

8
00:00:28,279 --> 00:00:30,569
(Past Sheldon:)It also faces the television
at a direct angle...

9
00:00:30,739 --> 00:00:33,739
(Past Sheldon:)...allowing me to immerse myself
in entertainment or game play...

10
00:00:33,909 --> 00:00:36,579
(Past Sheldon:)...without being subjected to conversation.
As a result...

11
00:00:36,745 --> 00:00:39,995
(Past Sheldon:)...I've placed it in a state of eternal dibs.

12
00:00:41,542 --> 00:00:42,792
(Past Leonard:)Can you do that?

13
00:00:43,669 --> 00:00:45,879
[SPEAKING FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

14
00:00:47,047 --> 00:00:49,887
That's Latin for "My chair my rules."

15
00:00:52,136 --> 00:00:57,476
(Past Sheldon:)Now, you said on the phone
that your area of study is physics.

